    "CPU bus/prefetch timing remains approximate. Both MOV and ROM-literal timer layouts agree with mGBA. The earlier two-cycle difference was mGBA multiboot auto-detection running a tiny fixture from EWRAM; padded cartridges remove that comparison mismatch.",
    "The internal CPU/reference PPU shares the hardware core. Independent mGBA verification covers the saved-room load/picture, specified timer microchecks, original BIOS pipeline/IRQ/cartridge-callback fixture and listed replacement-BIOS service observations.",
    "The MIT replacement BIOS remains incomplete. A supplied GBA BIOS separately passes the original fixed-rate, resampled and one-shot driver cases: selected service results and active mixer buffers agree with mGBA, while native/reference PCM agrees byte for byte. The independent comparison is scoped to mixer buffers and selected service results; final cross-core PCM is not bit-identical.",
    "Daily-clock checks read the original game state without patches or injected calls. Individual planted-berry growth and a full owner playthrough remain unqualified.",
    "The product downloads no firmware. A supplied BIOS was used privately for the optional sound-driver qualification; BIOS execution is interpreted and strict static mode rejects it.",
